# Corpus unit sample-specific-masks/C06 — justified (T2 exemplar: the all-CQs-met path)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/sample-specific-masks.yaml C06 (comparative, controlled_comparison;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: patch-wise interpolation upsamples CNN mask outputs at lower
# cost than bilinear/bicubic — pixel accesses 0.151e6 vs 0.602e6 vs 2.408e6, batch time
# 0.026+-0.004 s vs 0.062+-0.001 s vs 0.195+-0.013 s (ResNet-18/50, batch 256, A100), and no
# backprop through the upsampling step.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Nearest-competitor convention: the annotation quantifies over competitors
#     {bilinear, bicubic}; the unit's formal atom takes the CHEAPER competitor (bilinear) as B —
#     the binding comparison. Bicubic is dominated a fortiori under the reported ordering and
#     stays in `nl` and the leaf refs.
#   * All three mandatory corpus-v1 CQs are annotated met, including variance_reported (E06
#     Metrics: stds 0.004/0.001/0.013 are far smaller than the gaps) — the rare comparison claim
#     that clears the full bar, hence the justified exemplar.
#   * The annotation's optional fair-comparison CQ (downstream quality preserved, E03/E05) maps
#     onto corpus-v1's optional scope_match and is discharged.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact sample-specific-masks at sha256:d7bd879e0d54
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim ------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c06
  nl      = "Patch-wise interpolation upsamples sample-specific masks at lower cost than bilinear (and a fortiori bicubic): 0.151e6 vs 0.602e6 pixel accesses, 0.026 s vs 0.062 s per 256-image batch on A100, and no backprop through upsampling"
  formal  = better(patch_wise, bilinear, upsampling_cost, smm_resnet_a100)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: E06's cost comparison (pixel accesses, batch time, backprop-free), reported
# per result cell in the annotation and folded into this leaf's refs (per-result-cell grain).
leaf e1 : reports(e06, compares(patch_wise, bilinear, upsampling_cost, smm_resnet_a100, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C06, logic/experiments.md#E06-Metrics, logic/experiments.md#E06-Procedure-step-4]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(patch_wise, bilinear, e06)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E06-Setup]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(upsampling_cost, e06)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E06-Metrics]

leaf e4 : variance_reported(e06)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E06-Metrics]

leaf e5 : scope_matched(patch_wise, upsampling_cost, smm_resnet_a100)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03, logic/experiments.md#E05]

# --- The support argument ----------------------------------------------------------------------

arg a1 : supports(c06) by controlled_comparison(patch_wise, bilinear, upsampling_cost, smm_resnet_a100, e06)
  discharge baseline_parity      with e2
  discharge measurement_validity with e3
  discharge variance_reported    with e4
  discharge scope_match          with e5

status c06

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: a1 alone, unattacked -> in (grounded).
# Claim status:
#   c06 -> justified (its complete support a1 is `in`; spec §8 aggregation)
